<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Textbook-based Datasets</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A2.T10" title="Table 10 ‣ B.3 Textbook-based Datasets ‣ Appendix B Detailed Experimental Results ‣ More Data or Better Data? A Critical Analysis of Data Selection and Synthesis for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> illustrates the performance of models fine-tuned on the textbook-based datasets. Two datasets constructed with the same method result in significantly different performance gains for the model. We believe this is related to the data mixing strategy.</p>
</div>
